-for-14.\n\nThis is not a single-player rescue of a thin roster. It is a winning group with enough production to make the development question real. The Oaks buried Orlando early for their third straight win before surviving a tighter Philadelphia game with a fourth-quarter surge. The record is now 8-1, and the franchise stability line is growing. Those facts make Hayward’s progress consequential, but they do not prove that every promising performance should trigger a larger role immediately.\n\nThe next board read is therefore narrower than “can Hayward play?,can Hayward play?

